{"type":"text","timestamp":1790405893129,"sessionID":"ses_f238359adffeOkK22fccqsEEGl","part":{"id":"prt_0dc81dbfa0012wtqC9W30OdZI6","messageID":"msg_0dc80bb53001DiJmc4F5sgX9Lp","sessionID":"ses_f238359adffeOkK22fccqsEEGl","type":"text","text":"I’ll preserve the pointer-to-card offset during dragging, use a monotonic timestamp for the 50 ms release guard, and restore cards through `Hand` only when they actually left `Cards`. This avoids stale timer callbacks and keeps the initial base-state entry harmless.","time":{"start":1790405893114,"end":1790405893116},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0ed097b0ac3a76fb016ab76cf6178481948583495f6a07f94d","phase":"commentary"}}}}
